<article class="env-lemma" id="0HAP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0HAP">Lemma <span data-tag="0HAP">69.11.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a quasi-compact, separated, étale morphism of algebraic spaces. Then for any quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module $\mathcal{F}$ the map $f^*f_*\mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{F}$ is split. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Consider the cartesian diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \times _ Y X \ar[r]_-p \ar[d]_ q &  X \ar[d]^ f \\  X \ar[r]^ f &  Y }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       By Lemma <a href="/tag/07U8" data-tag="07U8">69.11.1</a> we have $f^*f_*\mathcal{F} = q_*p^*\mathcal{F}$. The morphism $\Delta : X \to X \times _ Y X$ is open (as a morphism between algebraic spaces étale over $Y$) and closed as $f$ is separated. Thus we see that $p^*\mathcal{F}$ is a direct sum of $\Delta _*\mathcal{F}$ and a quasi-coherent module supported on the (open and closed) complement of $\Delta (X)$. Tracing the maps the reader verifies that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{F} = q_*\Delta _*\mathcal{F} \to q_*p^*\mathcal{F} = f^*f_*\mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{F}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is the identity map. Details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>